event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":105,"item_id":"rs_08b9bfc9a3c6c295016ac93f73edb087d1b5b5a8b1e2026230","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Planning app backend**\n\nI need to implement a small app backend with static JavaScript routes that allow the browser to fetch data. I'll use Node for integration tests and temporary database persistence while handling 404 errors. SQLite will be synchronized. I’m considering modular app exports to create the server, ensuring it closes the database connection on the server close event for simpler tests. The main file will be server.js, and I’ll set up routes for health checks and project management while handling form validation. CSS will be included for a polished look."}

